==Latin==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From root {{term|op|lang=la}} in {{term|ops|lang=la}}.<!-- Century 1911 says: from root "op" in "optare" ("to choose") -->

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|lang=la|/ˈop.ti.mus/|[ˈɔp.tɨ.mʊs]|[ˈɔp.tʉ.mʊs]}}
* {{audio|la-cls-optimus.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-superlative|optimus|bonus|bonus}}

# best; good
#: ''Hic mundus perfectissimus est etiam mundorum possibilium omnium optimus''
#:* This most perfect world is even the best of all possible worlds ({{w|Immanuel Kant}}, echoing {{w|Leibniz}}).

